70: Work submitted to arXiv undergoes a series of quality assurance checks as part of cite83†moderation . This helps authors by ensuring their work will be discoverable and archivable and helps readers find relevant research that is in a consistent, readable format.\nL171: Quality assurance checks can take between one to four days to resolve, sometimes longer. Authors will be notified by email if any issues are found in the submission. Authors will also receive an email when the submission is posted publicly.\nL172: Submissions to arXiv are typically posted publicly Sunday through Thursday, with no announcements Friday or Saturday. You can check the cite88†current arXiv time†arxiv.org , which also shows the next deadline. Submissions are made public as part of the cite27†scheduled announcement process . This includes new submissions as well as cite35†replacements , cite44†withdrawal notices , cite30†cross listings and cite32†journal reference .\nL173: ## A note about arXiv-id assignments\nL174: \nL175: The final cite49†arXiv identifier is assigned as part of the automated process when the work is announced. It is not possible to generate or to be provided with the arXiv identifier or DOI in advance. Submitting authors will receive an email when the work is announced and it will appear on their account dashboard.\nL176: Note: The arXiv identifier cannot be back-dated, so identifiers will be assigned in the month of first announcement. It may be the case that a submission appears in a different identifier month than its original submission date due to various factors.\nL177: ## Announcement Schedule\nL178: Submissions received between\nL179: (all times Eastern US)  | Will be announced\nL180: (all times Eastern US)  | Mailed to subscribers\nL181: --- | --- | ---\nL182: Monday 14:00 – Tuesday 14:00  | Tuesday 20:00  | Tuesday night / Wednesday morning\nL183: Tuesday 14:00 – Wednesday 14:00  | Wednesday 20:00  | Wednesday night / Thursday morning\nL184: Wednesday 14:00 – Thursday 14:00  | Thursday 20:00  | Thursday night / Friday morning\nL185: Thursday 14:00 – Friday 14:00  | Sunday 20:00  | Sunday night / Monday morning\nL186: Friday 14:00 – Monday 14:00  | Monday 20:00  | Monday night / Tuesday morning\nL187: ## On Deferred Mailings\nL188: \nL189: Occasionally, arXiv defers a mailing, either for locally celebrated holidays such as Thanksgiving or for ad hoc reasons. Information about deferred mailings may be found on the cite89†arXiv status†status.arxiv.org page, or on the cite16†arXiv blog†blog.arxiv.org .\nL190: ### 2026 Holidays\nL191: \nL192:   * Thursday 2026-01-01\nL193:   * Monday 2026-01-19\nL194:   * Friday 2026-06-19\nL195:   * Friday 2026-07-03\nL196:   * Monday 2026-09-07\nL197:   * Thursday 2026-11-26\nL198:   * Friday 2026-12-25\nL199:   * Tuesday 2026-12-29\nL200:   * Thursday 2026-12-31\nL201: \nL202: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite90†member institutions , , and all contributors.\nL203: \nL204: cite91†About · cite92†Help · cite93†Contact · cite94†Subscribe · cite33†Copyright · cite80†Privacy · cite95†Accessibility · cite89†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L205: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResearch | OpenAI (https://openai.com/research/)\nciteturn25681view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://openai.com/research/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 141\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:   * [Button: Research]\nL3:   * [Button: Products]\nL4:   * [Button: Business]\nL5:   * [Button: Developers]\nL6:   * [Button: Company]\nL7:   * cite1†Foundation(opens in a new window)†openaifoundation.org L8: \nL9: cite2†Try ChatGPT(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com [Button: Login]\nL10: \nL11: OpenAI\nL12: \nL13: Research\nL14: # Pioneering research on the path to AGI\nL15: \nL16: We believe our research will eventually lead to artificial general intelligence, a system that can solve human-level problems. Our mission is to ensure that AGI benefits all of humanity.\nL17: \nL18: cite3†View research index cite4†Learn about safety L19: \nL20: Focus areas\nL21: \nL22: ### We advance the science of AI through research on frontier models, reasoning, multimodal systems, and safe deployment.\nL23: ### GPT\nL24: \nL25: OpenAI’s GPT series models are fast, versatile, and cost-efficient AI systems designed to understand context, generate content, and reason across text, images, and more.\nL26: \nL27: cite5†Complex coding and professional work at a lower cost ReleaseSep 29, 202612 min read L28: \nL29: cite6†GPT‑6 Astra: A new generation of intelligence ReleaseSep 3, 202628 min read L30: \nL31: cite7†More intelligence from every token for your hardest work ReleaseJul 9, 202618 min read L32: ### Visual\nL33: \nL34: Our research on visual and multimodal AI has led to advances in image generation, vision-language understanding, and models that can reason across images and text.\nL35: \nL36: cite8†Sharper details, faster generation, and more precise editing ChatGPT Images 2.5Sep 8, 20266 min read L37: \nL38: cite9†A state-of-the-art model that makes precise, immediately usable visuals ChatGPT Images 2.0Apr 21, 202611 min read L39: cite10†A natively multimodal model capable of precise, accurate, photorealistic outputs 4o Image GenerationMar 25, 20256 min read L40: ### Audio\nL41: \nL42: Our research on applying AI to audio processing and audio generation has led to advances in speech recognition, real-time speech generation, and models that can listen and respond simultaneously.\nL43: \nL44: cite11†Natural, real-time conversations with AI GPT-LiveJul 8, 202610 min read L45: \nL46: cite12†Navigating the challenges and opportunities of synthetic voices Voice EngineMar 29, 20248 min read L47: \nL48: cite13†Approaching human-level robustness and accuracy on English speech recognition WhisperSep 21, 20222 min read L49: ### Featured roles\nL50: \nL51: We are actively seeking talented individuals to join our team. Explore featured roles or view all open roles.\nL52: \nL53: cite14†View all careers L54: ## Explore all research\nL55: \nL56: cite3†View research index L57: \nL58: Research\nL59: \nL60:   * cite3†Research Index L61:   * cite15†Research Overview L62:   * cite16†Economic Research L63: \nL64: Latest Advancements\nL65: \nL66:   * cite5†GPT-6.1 Sol L67:   * cite6†GPT-6 Astra L68:   * cite7†GPT-5.6 L69:   * cite17†GPT-5.5 L70: \nL71: Safety\nL72: \nL73:   * cite4†Safety Approach L74:   * cite18†Deployment Safety(opens in a new window)†deploymentsafety.openai.com L75:   * cite19†Security & Privacy L76:   * cite20†Trust & Transparency L77: \nL78: Products\nL79:   * cite2†ChatGPT(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L80:   * cite21†ChatGPT Business(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L81:   * cite22†ChatGPT Enterprise(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L82:   * cite23†ChatGPT for Education(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L83:   * cite24†Codex†chatgpt.com L84:   * cite25†Dots(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L85:   * cite26†Release Notes L86: \nL87: API Platform\nL88: \nL89:   * cite27†Overview L90:   * cite28†API Log In(opens in a new window)†platform.openai.com L91:   * cite29†Docs(opens in a new window)†developers.openai.com L92: \nL93: Business\nL94:   * cite30†Overview L95:   * cite31†Solutions L96:   * cite32†Resources L97:   * cite33†Plugins L98:   * cite34†Customer Stories L99:   * cite35†Partner Network L100:   * cite36†Contact Sales L101: \nL102: Developers\nL103: \nL104:   * cite37†Apps SDK(opens in a new window)†developers.openai.com L105:   * cite38†Open Models L106:   * cite39†Docs(opens in a new window)†developers.openai.com L107:   * cite40†Resources(opens in a new wi